## Background jobs

ARQ runs background jobs against Redis. The worker configuration lives in
`{{ spec.package }}.worker.WorkerSettings`, and the example task in
`{{ spec.package }}.tasks.example` shows the expected `ctx` and argument
signature. Start the worker from the project root:

```sh
uv run arq {{ spec.package }}.worker.WorkerSettings
```

The worker reads `REDIS_URL` through `RedisSettings.from_dsn` and registers
`example_task` in `WorkerSettings.functions`.
