## Rate limiting

The application installs a SlowAPI limiter as `app.state.limiter` with a default
limit of 100 requests per minute. The `/limited` endpoint demonstrates a tighter
limit of 5 requests per minute. Exceeding a limit returns `429` with a JSON
`detail` field.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("uploads") %}

## File uploads

Uploads are stored through the `Storage` protocol in
`{{ spec.package }}.core.storage`. The default `LocalStorage` backend writes to
`UPLOAD_DIR` (`uploads` by default) and creates missing parent directories.

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/uploads` | Store a file after checking its type and size and return `201` with a generated `key`. |
| `GET` | `/uploads/{key}` | Download a stored file or return `404`. |
| `DELETE` | `/uploads/{key}` | Delete a stored file and return `204`. |

`MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES` defaults to `5000000`. `ALLOWED_UPLOAD_TYPES` lists the
accepted media types and defaults to PNG, JPEG, PDF, and plain text. Rejected
types return `415`; oversized files return `413`. Stored keys are generated on
the server and resolved below the configured directory, so path traversal
attempts are rejected.

```sh
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/uploads" \
  -F "file=@example.png;type=image/png"

curl "http://127.0.0.1:8000/uploads/<key>"

curl -X DELETE "http://127.0.0.1:8000/uploads/<key>"
```
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("s3") %}

## S3-compatible storage

Set `STORAGE_BACKEND=s3` to use `S3Storage` instead of the local backend. The
backend calls `boto3` in a worker thread so the event loop stays responsive.
Configure the bucket with `S3_BUCKET`, the region with `S3_REGION`, and an
optional custom endpoint with `S3_ENDPOINT_URL`. Leave the endpoint empty for
AWS S3; set it for providers such as MinIO. `S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and
`S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` are empty by default, so the standard AWS credential
chain is used when they are unset.

```sh
STORAGE_BACKEND=s3 S3_BUCKET=uploads S3_REGION=us-east-1 uv run fastapi dev src/{{ spec.package }}/main.py
```
{% endif %}
