## Kubernetes

The `k8s/` directory contains a Deployment, Service, ConfigMap, and Ingress.
Replace `ghcr.io/example/{{ spec.name }}:latest` with your published image and
set the ingress host `{{ spec.name }}.example.com` to a domain you control before
deploying.

The Deployment exposes port `8000`, reads `ENVIRONMENT` and `LOG_LEVEL` from the
ConfigMap, and uses `/ready` for readiness and `/health` for liveness probes. The
Service listens on port `80` and forwards to port `8000`. Apply the manifests
with:

```sh
kubectl apply -f k8s/configmap.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/service.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/ingress.yaml
```
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("ci-gitlab") %}

## GitLab CI

`.gitlab-ci.yml` uses the `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.13.6` image and runs three
stages: `lint`, `typecheck`, and `test`. Each job runs `uv sync` first, then Ruff
format and lint checks, mypy, pyright, or pytest. The pipeline starts
automatically when the repository is hosted on GitLab.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("ci-bitbucket") %}

## Bitbucket Pipelines

`bitbucket-pipelines.yml` uses `python:{{ spec.python }}-slim`, installs `uv`,
runs `uv sync`, and then executes Ruff format and lint checks, mypy, pyright, and
pytest. Enable Pipelines for the repository in Bitbucket to run it.
